      "text": "To \"cite\" (cross-reference) a table in your text, you use the **`\\ref`** command. \n\nSince your table already has the line `\\label{tab:organ-metabolizers}`, you are all set to reference it. Here are the three most common ways to do it:\n\n### 1. The Standard Way (Built-in)\nIn the text where you want to mention the table, type:\n```latex\nAs seen in Table~\\ref{tab:organ-metabolizers}, the small intestine...\n```\n*   **The `~` (tilde):** This is a \"non-breaking space.\" It ensures that \"Table\" and \"1\" never get split across two different lines.\n\n### 2. The \"Smart\" Way (Using `cleveref`)\nIf you want LaTeX to automatically type the word \"Table\" for you (and capitalize it correctly), use the **`cleveref`** package.\n\n**In your preamble:**\n```latex\n\\usepackage[noabbrev]{cleveref} % Load this AFTER hyperref if you use it\n```\n\n**In your text:**\n```latex\n% Use lowercase \\cref for the middle of sentences\nThe data in \\cref{tab:organ-metabolizers} shows... \n% Output: The data in table 1 shows...\n\n% Use uppercase \\Cref for the start of sentences\n\\Cref{tab:organ-metabolizers} outlines the organs... \n% Output: Table 1 outlines the organs...\n```\n\n### 3. The Clickable Way (Using `hyperref`)\nIf you want the table number to be a clickable blue link in your PDF, add this to your preamble:\n```latex\n\\usepackage{hyperref}\n```\nIf you use this with the standard `\\ref`, only the number \"1\" will be clickable. If you use it with `cleveref`, the entire \"Table 1\" text becomes a link.\n\n---\n\n### Pro-Tip: Label Placement\nIn your original code, you have the `\\label` right under the `\\caption`. **This is correct.** \n\nIn LaTeX, the `\\label` **must** come after (or inside) the `\\caption` command. If you put it before the caption, LaTeX will accidentally reference the Section number instead of the Table number.",
